  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch Local Colombian Cheese</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the Gouda Cheese Development B.V. is to create an inclusive business model in Antioquia, Colombia with a local milk-farmers&#x2019; cooperative and add value to their existing milk-chain, making Gouda cheese, using the know-how and technology from the Netherlands. With the help of DGGF-TA they were able to start a pilot project leading to a well-functioning cheese production site. This local cooperation has led to a vast local community of farmers being involved with the making of the cheese, as well as being trained to improve the quality of their milk. The company focuses on providing jobs for young people from the countryside as well as employing females for the production of the cheese. 50 farmers are supplying milk for cheese production, leading to 23 indirect supported FTE, at the factory itself 3 FTE have been created related to the production and sales of the cheese and a total of 120 people have been trained during the course of the pilot.</narrative>
  </description>
